WEBVTT

00:00:00.256 --> 00:00:04.631
Cluster A has a saved record, but that record is not a live health check.

00:00:04.736 --> 00:00:08.897
Review the PE endpoint, expected UUID, complete node

00:00:08.917 --> 00:00:10.925
baseline and credential reference.

00:00:11.051 --> 00:00:13.391
Select Collect PE health deliberately.

00:00:13.509 --> 00:00:18.012
The operational-health collector offers a per-collection PE TLS exception for

00:00:18.032 --> 00:00:20.872
deployment and recovery. Record its reason.

00:00:21.104 --> 00:00:25.308
HTTPS remains encrypted, but the exception does not authenticate the

00:00:25.328 --> 00:00:29.763
PE certificate. The observation retains this policy and is not labelled

00:00:29.783 --> 00:00:31.392
certificate-verified evidence.

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:35.289
If collection fails, read the specific diagnostic.

00:00:35.458 --> 00:00:39.348
Untrusted issuer and certificate address mismatch have different fixes.

00:00:39.522 --> 00:00:43.919
An unresolved reference differs from HTTP four zero one authentication

00:00:43.959 --> 00:00:47.012
rejection or four zero three access denial.

00:00:47.202 --> 00:00:51.619
DNS, timeout, refused connection and routing errors describe transport

00:00:51.639 --> 00:00:55.108
failures. None of these alone proves an unhealthy cluster.

00:00:55.405 --> 00:00:58.692
A completed observation expires after fifteen minutes.

00:00:58.946 --> 00:01:03.278
Evidence age uses the appliance timestamps, while browser clock skew

00:01:03.298 --> 00:01:04.950
produces a separate warning.

00:01:05.105 --> 00:01:09.161
A workstation timezone display is not itself proof of clock drift.

00:01:09.329 --> 00:01:13.875
Correct invalid or future timestamps and time synchronization before relying

00:01:13.895 --> 00:01:18.448
on the result. Use Live Prism Element drift to compare the supported settings

00:01:18.532 --> 00:01:20.368
against an approved baseline.

00:01:20.622 --> 00:01:23.355
Test the comparison manually before scheduling it.

00:01:23.481 --> 00:01:27.397
Keep a failed collection distinct from a real configuration difference.

00:01:27.596 --> 00:01:32.013
A schedule needs the same valid credentials, reachability and trust as the

00:01:32.033 --> 00:01:35.491
manual check. Refresh only reloads saved records;

00:01:35.532 --> 00:01:37.518
it does not collect Prism data.

00:01:37.665 --> 00:01:41.961
Review timestamps, source and the individual checks before acceptance.

00:01:42.156 --> 00:01:46.638
A PE Good readback is not a full NCC, resilience, application

00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:48.836
or recovery acceptance test.

00:01:49.068 --> 00:01:53.409
Close historical attention reviews deliberately after investigating their source.
